<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xsd:schema xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:jaxb="https://jakarta.ee/xml/ns/jaxb" xmlns:nxe="http://www.ndg.com/xmleditor/1.0.0"
	xmlns:map="http://www.ndg.com/map" targetNamespace="http://www.ndg.com/map"
	jaxb:version="3.0">

	<!-- Map coordinate spaces and rules for traversing between adjacent coordinates -->
	 
	<xsd:simpleType name="coordinateSystemType">
		<xsd:restriction base="xsd:normalizedString">
			<xsd:enumeration value="S"><xsd:annotation>
				<xsd:documentation>
Square coordinate system
Direction '1' is straight up, '2' is up-right, '3' is right and so in a clockwise fashion
-------------------------------------
| 0,0 | 1,0 | 2,0 | 3,0 | 4,0 |....
-------------------------------------
| 0,1 | 1,1 | 2,1 | 3,1 | 4,1 |....
-------------------------------------
| 0,2 | 1,2 | 2,2 | 3,2 | 4,2 |....
-------------------------------------
   ...     ...     ...     ...     ...    ...
   				</xsd:documentation>
				<xsd:appinfo><jaxb:typesafeEnumMember name="SQUARE"/></xsd:appinfo>
			</xsd:annotation></xsd:enumeration>
			
			<xsd:enumeration value="H"><xsd:annotation>
				<xsd:documentation>
Hex coordinate system
Direction '1' is straight up, '2' is up-right, '3' is down-right and so in a clockwise fashion
 ___     ___       ___
/0,0\__/2,0\___/4,0\  ...
\___/1,0\_ /3,0\___/
/0,1 \__/2,1\__/4,1\  ...
\___/1,1\_ /3,1\___/
/0,2 \__/2,2\__/4,2\  ...
\___/1,2\_ /3,2\___/
      \___/  \___/
 ...    ...  ...  ...   ...   ...
				</xsd:documentation>
				<xsd:appinfo><jaxb:typesafeEnumMember name="HEX"/></xsd:appinfo>
			</xsd:annotation></xsd:enumeration>
			
			<xsd:enumeration value="V"><xsd:annotation>
				<xsd:documentation>
Vertical hex coordinate system
Direction '1' is up-right, '2' is right, '3' is down-right, '4' is down-left, '5' is left, '6' is up-left
 /  \  /  \ /  \  /  \ 
|0,0|1,0|2,0|3,0|
 \  /  \  / \  /  \  / 
  |0,1 |1,1 |2,1|
 /  \  /  \ /  \  /  \
|0,2|1,2|2,2|3,2|
 \  /  \  / \  /  \  / 
 ...    ...  ...  ...   ...   ...
				</xsd:documentation>
				<xsd:appinfo><jaxb:typesafeEnumMember name="VERTICAL_HEX"/></xsd:appinfo>
			</xsd:annotation></xsd:enumeration>
			
			<xsd:enumeration value="D"><xsd:annotation>
				<xsd:documentation>
Diamond coordinate system
Although this is basically a square coordinate system tilted by 45 degrees, Direction '1' is still straight up, '2' is up-right, '3' is right and so in a clockwise fashion
Diamond maps don't support wrapping
  / \   / \    / \   / \    / \
/0,0\/1,0\/2,0\/3,0\/4,0\      ...
\    /\     /\    /\     /\    / \
  \/0,1\/1,1\/2,1\/3,1\/4,1\   ...
  / \   / \    / \   / \    / \   /
/0,2\/1,2\/2,2\/3,2\/4,2\/    ...
\    /\     /\    /\     /\    / \
  \/0,3\/1,3\/2,3\/3,3\/4,3\   ...
  / \   / \    / \   / \    / \   /
/0,4\/1,4\/2,4\/3,4\/4,4\/    ...
\    /\     /\    /\     /\    /
  \/    \ /    \/    \ /    \/

  ...    ...   ...    ...    ...        ...
				</xsd:documentation>
				<xsd:appinfo><jaxb:typesafeEnumMember name="DIAMOND"/></xsd:appinfo>
			</xsd:annotation></xsd:enumeration>
			
			<xsd:enumeration value="W"><xsd:annotation>
				<xsd:documentation>
Wrapped diamond coordinate system
Looks the same as regular diamond coordinate system, but the tiles are numbered differently
To use this, its mandatory that "wraps left to right" is turned on, and "wraps top to bottom" can optionally be on
  / \   / \    / \   / \    / \
/0,0\/1,0\/2,0\/3,0\/4,0\      ...
\    /\     /\    /\     /\    / \
  \/0,1\/1,1\/2,1\/3,1\/4,1\   ...
  / \   / \    / \   / \    / \   /
/9,2\/0,2\/1,2\/2,2\/3,2\/    ...
\    /\     /\    /\     /\    / \
  \/9,3\/0,3\/1,3\/2,3\/3,3\   ...
  / \   / \    / \   / \    / \   /
/8,4\/9,4\/0,4\/1,4\/2,4\/    ...
\    /\     /\    /\     /\    /
  \/    \ /    \/    \ /    \/

  ...    ...   ...    ...    ...        ...
				</xsd:documentation>
				<xsd:appinfo><jaxb:typesafeEnumMember name="WRAPPED_DIAMOND"/></xsd:appinfo>
			</xsd:annotation></xsd:enumeration>
		</xsd:restriction>
	</xsd:simpleType>

	<xsd:complexType name="mapCoordinates2D">
        <xsd:sequence>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1" name="x" type="map:mapDimension"/>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1" name="y" type="map:mapDimension"/>
        </xsd:sequence>
	</xsd:complexType>
	
	<xsd:complexType name="mapCoordinates3D">
		<xsd:complexContent>
			<xsd:extension base="map:mapCoordinates2D">
		        <xsd:sequence>
					<xsd:element minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1" name="z" type="map:mapDimension"/>
        		</xsd:sequence>
        	</xsd:extension>
        </xsd:complexContent>
	</xsd:complexType>
	
	<xsd:complexType name="coordinateSystem">
        <xsd:annotation>
        	<xsd:documentation>Defines a coordinate space with boundaries and the rules for traversing from one cell to adjacent cells.</xsd:documentation>
        </xsd:annotation>
		<xsd:sequence>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1" name="coordinateSystemType" type="map:coordinateSystemType" nxe:label="Coordinate system type" nxe:showmaincolumn="false" />
			<xsd:element minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1" name="width" type="map:mapDimension" nxe:label="Width" nxe:gridwidth="60" />
			<xsd:element minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1" name="height" type="map:mapDimension" nxe:label="Height" nxe:gridwidth="60" />
			<xsd:element minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1" name="depth" type="map:mapDimension" nxe:label="Depth" nxe:gridwidth="60">
			    <xsd:annotation>
    				<xsd:documentation>Ignored when dealing with 2D maps.</xsd:documentation>
				</xsd:annotation>
			</xsd:element>
			<xsd:element minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1" name="wrapsLeftToRight" type="xsd:boolean" nxe:label="Wraps Left-Right?" nxe:gridwidth="120" />
			<xsd:element minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1" name="wrapsTopToBottom" type="xsd:boolean" nxe:label="Wraps Top-Bottom?" nxe:gridwidth="120" />
		</xsd:sequence>
	</xsd:complexType>
	
	<xsd:simpleType name="mapDimension">
		<xsd:restriction base="xsd:unsignedShort" />
	</xsd:simpleType>
	
	<xsd:simpleType name="mapDirection">
	    <xsd:annotation>
    		<xsd:documentation>Map direction 1..8, 1 being north, 2 being north-east and so on.</xsd:documentation>
		</xsd:annotation>
		<xsd:restriction base="xsd:unsignedShort">
			<xsd:minInclusive value="1"/>
			<xsd:maxInclusive value="8"/>
		</xsd:restriction>
	</xsd:simpleType>
	
</xsd:schema>